"""German -> English glossary for the VW / Audi K-matrix names in opendbc (vw_pq, vw_mqb, vw_mqbevo, vw_mlb).

Keys are lower case with umlauts written out (ae oe ue ss), the way the DBCs spell them. Values are the English word as
it should appear inside an identifier (CamelCase pieces, no spaces). dbc_tool.py splits compounds into these stems
("Kuehlmitteltemperatur" -> kuehlmittel + temperatur -> CoolantTemperature), so a stem here covers every compound
built from it. Grow it from the "untranslated" report that `dbc_tool.py translate` writes.

KEEP: abbreviations that stay as they are (ECU / function prefixes of the K-matrix, units, English words that would
otherwise be split into German stems).
"""

